  "ingredients": [
    "0.75 cup cool water, divided",
    "1/4 teaspoon liquid rennet",
    "1.5 teaspoons citric acid",
    "1 gallon raw milk",
    "1 teaspoon salt"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Combine 1/4 cup water and rennet in a small bowl; mix well.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine remaining 1/2 cup water and citric acid in another small bowl; mix until dissolved.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour milk into a large pot set over medium heat. Stir in citric acid mixture.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat milk, stirring occasionally, until it registers 90 degrees F (32 degrees C) on an instant-read thermometer, about 5 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/uUnU3oh1qwTBs1Ob28q3GEaOvTI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/254478-homemade-mozzarella-cheese-ddmfs-step-01-428e26b5f3384c56911bfd3f2660a2fc.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/254478/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove milk from heat and stir in rennet mixture in a figure-8 motion for 30 seconds. Stir counterclockwise for 30 seconds to still the milk. Let stand, covered, until milk sets into curd, 5 to 10 minutes. Press edge of curd gently with a palette knife or the back of a spoon to check for firmness.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/7AZJH032pzvtPysvxWq_ZUzTtE4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/254478-homemade-mozzarella-cheese-ddmfs-step-02-84ddb7ccc2b84711acd3aa8989ebe10f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/254478/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice vertically into the pot to cut curd into 3/4-inch cubes with a palette knife. Stir curds gently, but leave cubes mostly intact.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/1-3S0w4nhINxYOY8nBowirXw2-k=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/254478-homemade-mozzarella-cheese-ddmfs-step-03-a06daeb2d43c4518bad4f77c188daf95.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/254478/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Return pot to the heat; cook over medium heat, stirring curds gently, until temperature reaches 109 degrees F (43 degrees C), about 5 minutes. Remove from heat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/85antObyyWRGHxZUUPsypFweKbs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/254478-homemade-mozzarella-cheese-ddmfs-step-04-277eca96af6f45a8b08c6f8e401ee5c7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/254478/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ladle curds into a colander set over a large bowl using a slotted spoon. Press curds gently to extract liquid whey. Pour drained whey back into the pot.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/qoH3HRrG_WR_GH6uCIEGTmdUnU4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/254478-homemade-mozzarella-cheese-ddmfs-step-05-e099bcc9957046f5834f390d9056debc.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/254478/step_08.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat whey to 185 degrees F (85 degrees C), about 5 minutes. Wearing gloves, tear off a piece of curd and place on a slotted spoon. Dip curd into hot whey for 5 to 10 seconds. Stretch, fold, and knead curd. Repeat until mozzarella is smooth and elastic. Knead in salt and form curd into a ball. Repeat dipping and kneading process with remaining curd.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/vw3blUqniPA4s-1k8H1C58kYEvg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/254478-homemade-mozzarella-cheese-ddmfs-step-06-115bc6d24bd74d74a1226d353fe9d134.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/254478/step_09.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Allow mozzarella to cool. Wrap tightly in plastic wrap and transfer to the refrigerator.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/1HUiqCT2-XjREOi7PB_geWjPMF0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/254478-homemade-mozzarella-cheese-DDMFS-4x3-ed982c4254fe4d86bc38df6381729673.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/254478/step_11.webp"
    }
  ],
